# Platform folders

Each platform owns one root folder. Never mix them.

| Plan | Code | Plan docs |
|------|------|-----------|
| Android phone | `android/` | `execution plan/android/` |
| iOS | `iOS/` | `execution plan/iOS/` |
| iPadOS | `iPadOS/` | `execution plan/iPadOS/` |
| Android tablet | `AndroidTablet/` | `execution plan/AndroidTablet/` |
| macOS | `macOS/` | `execution plan/macOS/` |
| Windows | `Windows/` | `execution plan/Windows/` |
| Linux | `Linux/` | `execution plan/Linux/` |

- Change files only under the platform the user named, plus `desktop-core/` when that phase explicitly requires shared Rust.
- Do not create a new platform root. Do not copy business logic into a platform folder to satisfy isolation.
- Do not modify `android/` unless the user explicitly asks. Android may be read as the UI reference.
- Follow `execution plan/<platform>/` (`design.md`, `requirements.md`, `editor-rules.md`). Do not invent a different product, including a CLI shell, when the plan requires a real UI.
- Linux and macOS have backend crates only. Their product UI has not been started. Do not treat a leftover shell as the UI.
